# Build-context exclusions for the GourMate backend image on Railway.
#
# Railway's Dockerfile builder uses the service root (this repository root) as
# the Docker build context, so it reads THIS file rather than
# backend/.dockerignore. Patterns are depth-agnostic (`**/`) so they match from
# the repository root; the backend/Dockerfile consumes `backend/...` paths.

# Python bytecode / caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/*.egg-info/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
**/.venv/
venv/
**/venv/

# Secrets / local env — never ship, but keep the documented template
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Tests & dev tooling
**/tests/
**/test/
**/conftest.py
**/pytest.ini
**/tox.ini
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# Frontend is deployed separately (Vercel); keep it out of the API image.
frontend/

# Tooling / VCS / docs
**/.git/
**/.github/
**/*.md
**/.DS_Store
